/-
AtFullSide/K13/CoinsTieFive.lean: kind K13, the members' batching: UNDER THE LIBRARY's HEAD h: THE
KIND's TIE `CoinsTie` AT THE BORDER 355 FROM FIVE PREMISES: KIND K1's RECORD OF PREMISES AT THE
OPENING (`K1Seated`) · the library's "opened" · THE JOB's PLAN AND RIDE ARE THE OPENING's · "THE
THREAD's BOOK IS THE ONE THAT THE MAKER `bookWhole` RETURNS" AT THE HEAD's OWN SENDINGS OF THE FIRST
CHAIN. THE RECORD IS A PREMISE: no Script is laid. THAT THE MAKER RETURNS THE THREAD's BOOK IS A
PREMISE: under h it does return a book at the head's own three lists of sendings
(`bookWhole_same_at_made`, Honest/K14/BookForAtPure.lean, at `bookWhole_returns_written`,
AtFullSide/K14/BookWholeWritten.lean); what is left is that the thread's book is that book.
Statements with their proofs, three of them closed facts by Lean's kernel; no definition. THE FULL
SIZE AND THE FORMAT's EARLIER HASH ALONE.

Main names: `shapeFourW`: the library's written list of the first chain's messages' shapes has, at
number 4, the shape of message number 4 of the opening's written plan; `shapeFourW_bites`: at number
3 it has not. `freeFourW`: at the written plan that message has 255 free mask entries.
`k13_hshape_at_head`: **under h and O: the listed shape at number 4 is that of message number 4 of
the opening's plan at the description's own ground.** `k13_free0_at_head`: **under h: the index
masks' ledger, as it is made, has 255 free entries.** `k13_coinsTie_of_five`: **the tie.**

What is gained. `k13_coinsTie_of_seated_written` (CoinsTieWritten.lean of this folder) has three
public premises on numbers: hshape, hfreeP, hfree. HERE ALL THREE ARE GONE: OF THESE THREE NONE IS
LEFT; a public count stays inside the record (its field hasCoins, which the proof beneath spends;
firstNo and treesNo are asked and not spent). And hW is asked at the head's own sendings of the
first chain, `Zp.made.proof.1`, which under h are the written ones; p1 and p2, the other two chains'
sendings, are free letters, tied to nothing: the statement holds at all of them.

WHAT IS LEFT, BESIDE h: FIVE; NONE IS SHOWN HERE. K: the record: twenty fields, of which the proof
beneath spends four (seats, msgs, fits, hasCoins; under hP and hR the field fits is no debt: K1's
`fits_two_head`, Honest/K1/Law/FitsWritten.lean, has it under h and O); its field `msgs` is the tie
between the Script and the sender's text. O: the library's "opened" at the seated description (under
h there is one: the field `opened` of `h.laid`, Johnson/P5J/LaidOpens.lean; it is a letter here
because hP and hR name its base). hP, hR: the job's plan and ride are the opening's at the
description's own ground: whoever lays the job pays both: where J is a job that `placeJob` makes, hP
is that text's field and hR is K1's `ride_of_job` (Honest/K1/Law/StartAtFour.lean); from the ground
at which a prover is laid to the description's own, Bs.G₀, is a further step, not treated here. hW:
`bookWhole` returns the thread's book, at the list `mergesByName`. OF ITS ROAD, NOT IMPORTED HERE:
`bookWhole_same_at_made` (Honest/K14/BookForAtPure.lean) at `bookWhole_returns_written`
(AtFullSide/K14/BookWholeWritten.lean) gives, under h alone, "there is a book B" with hW's own
equation at p1, p2 := the head's two other lists and B in Bk's place; these files' own limits bind.
Where the frame's maker `onlineProverFromPublicFiles` returns, its own book is that B (`atPure_book_at_head`,
Honest/K14/AtPureBookAtHead.lean). LEFT: Bk is the letter at which the Script, the thread and the
record K are typed: that these can be had at that B.

How. The library's `AtMg.msgs_at_head` and `AtMg.indexNo_at` (Johnson/P5J/PlanSitsCore.lean: the
list of shapes is the written one; the index masks' message is number 4), `codes_in_scope` and
`free_full` (Johnson/Desc/Sound/K11Tests/LettersSevenInScope.lean: the codes are the written ones;
255), `eG_atAll` (Johnson/Desc/K1/Law/TiesAtAll.lean: the opening's plan is the written one),
`sends_in_scope` (Johnson/Goal/Numbers/MadeInScope.lean: the sendings are the written ones); the
premise on the public data that three of these ask (`codes_in_scope`, `eG_atAll`, `sends_in_scope`)
is had under h by `pin1_atAll` (Johnson/Desc/K1/Law/PinsAtHead.lean); this kind's `m3_kCol`
(Honest/K13/GuardsAtM3.lean: 18 column variables): 13 + 37 is at most 255. `shapeFourW` and
`freeFourW`: by evaluation.

Limits. NOT IN FRONT OF A LAW OVER COINS: the ground: the Limits of Honest/K13/CoinsTieOfFacts.lean.
CONDITIONAL ON h AND THE FIVE PREMISES: that they hold together is not shown: hW AND THE RECORD's
FIELD hasCoins SPEAK OF ONE BOOK, AND DO NOT CLASH: under h, O, hP and hR the field follows from hW
by three statements of kind K1's, which no one statement joins at a book that is a letter:
`book_pick` and `rows_alike_head` (Honest/K1/Law/HasCoinsAtBook.lean: where the maker returns, the
book's first table begins with the rows that `rowsIn` yields; under h these are the written
description's) and `hasCoins_head_of` (Honest/K1/Law/HasCoinsOfRows.lean); none is imported here,
and the field stays asked inside K. hW fixes the book as the maker's value: it brings no guard and
no budget; the book is made without a look at the prover's parts. AT THE LIST `mergesByName`: THE
MAKER's GUESS which masked sumchecks are merges; compared with no program. A book's number is a
claim on a sender's text: here the two meet at written numbers, each by its own evaluation: no law
joins the texts. The limits of CoinsTieWritten.lean and WantsAtHead.lean of this folder and of
Honest/K13/CoinsTieOfSeated.lean and Honest/K13/StretchAtHead.lean bind here too: the thread stands
at the one input w₁ alone; where it holds nowhere all holds for nothing. WHERE `lendRow` ERRS AT THE
KIND's ROW THE TIE HOLDS FOR NOTHING TOO: at the book that `bookWhole` returns at the head's own
three lists of sendings it returns, under h (`k13_lendRow_at_head`, LendRowAtHead.lean of this
folder; not imported here); at other p1, p2 nothing is said. The verifier's taking, the tie's third
condition, returns under h wherever the thread stands at 355 (`k13_guard_taken`,
Honest/K13/GuardsAtM3.lean). (One limit of Honest/K13/CoinsTieAtHead.lean is overtaken here: under
h, O and hP the sending's table of codes and the verifier's are both the written one.) IT SAYS NO
MORE THAN ITS PREMISES: the record holds the tie between the Script and the sender's text, hW the
book. `shapeFourW` does not say that the plan has a message number 4 (`shapeAt` has a default); in
the tie that comes from the record. Three evaluations in Lean's kernel, which no independent checker
has replayed; 255 stands by three evaluations (`free_full`, `freeFourW`, the written owner's field
free): no law joins them. This file's imports reach Johnson/Goal/. Nothing outside this file calls
these statements.

What is not claimed. That any premise holds. It is none of the library's goals. Nothing on
soundness, completeness or hiding.
-/
import AtFullSide.K13.CoinsTieWritten
